{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe overestimation bias: The model consistently forecasts a smooth, monotonic recovery to ~85-90 EUR, ignoring the actual market's sharp volatility and failure to sustain levels above 82 EUR for extended periods. Apply a downward correction of 3-5 EUR to all forecast horizons.",
    "Account for extreme mean reversion lag: The model fails to capture the rapid drop from 91.72 to 78.15 and the subsequent oscillation. Forecasts should be adjusted to reflect a 'stuck' lower range (78-84 EUR) rather than a steady climb, delaying any projected recovery by at least 10-15 days.",
    "Ignore weak sentiment signals: Positive sentiment spikes (0.40-0.50) in the history did not trigger the sustained price increases predicted by the model. Treat sentiment values >0.30 as noise rather than leading indicators for upward momentum in this specific volatility regime.",
    "Reduce overshoot on recovery attempts: When the true price attempts to recover (e.g., days 17-19 in the outcome), the model's forecast is too aggressive. Cap the projected peak at 86-87 EUR instead of the model's 90+ EUR target.",
    "Apply higher volatility bands: The model's narrow forecast range (e.g., 81.60 to 85.54) is unrealistic compared to the true outcome's swings (79.81 to 90.16). Adjust forecasts to include wider daily variance, specifically anticipating sudden drops of 2-3 EUR even during apparent recovery phases."
  ]
}
